Installs the requests library (only needed once, not inside your script).

This is the library used to send HTTP requests to Google’s API.

import requests
import json


requests → sends HTTP POST/GET requests.

json → handles JSON data (Google API sends responses in JSON format).

API_KEY = "YOUR_GOOGLE_API_KEY"  # get from Google Cloud Console


You need to replace "YOUR_GOOGLE_API_KEY" with your actual API key from Google Cloud Console.

This key authenticates your program so Google allows you to use the Safe Browsing API.

url_to_check = "http://testsafebrowsing.appspot.com/s/phishing.html"


The website URL you want to test.

Here, Google provides a test phishing link.

You can replace this with any real URL (e.g., "https://example.com").

safe_browsing_url = f"https://safebrowsing.googleapis.com/v4/threatMatches:find?key={API_KEY}"


The endpoint (API URL) for Google Safe Browsing v4.

f"" is a formatted string → it inserts your API key into the URL.

Example:

https://safebrowsing.googleapis.com/v4/threatMatches:find?key=AIza...

payload = {
    "client": {
        "clientId": "yourcompanyname",
        "clientVersion": "1.0"
    },
    "threatInfo": {
        "threatTypes": ["MALWARE", "SOCIAL_ENGINEERING", "POTENTIALLY_HARMFUL_APPLICATION", "THREAT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"],
        "platformTypes": ["ANY_PLATFORM"],
        "threatEntryTypes": ["URL"],
        "threatEntries": [
            {"url": url_to_check}
        ]
    }
}

This is the request body (payload) you send to Google:

client → identifies your app. You can put any name/version here.

threatInfo → defines what you want Google to check:

threatTypes: types of dangers to check for:

"MALWARE" → malicious software

"SOCIAL_ENGINEERING" → phishing / scams

"POTENTIALLY_HARMFUL_APPLICATION" → bad apps

"THREAT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED" → general check

platformTypes: "ANY_PLATFORM" (works for all OS/browsers).

threatEntryTypes: "URL" (we are checking a website URL).

threatEntries: the actual URL(s) you want to check (here just one, url_to_check).

response = requests.post(safe_browsing_url, json=payload)


Sends an HTTP POST request to Google’s Safe Browsing API.

json=payload means Python will send the payload dictionary as JSON data in the request body.

The response from Google will say whether the site is safe or dangerous.

result = response.json()


Converts the API’s JSON response into a Python dictionary (result).

Example of response if dangerous:

{
  "matches": [
    {
      "threatType": "SOCIAL_ENGINEERING",
      "platformType": "ANY_PLATFORM",
      "threat": {"url": "http://testsafebrowsing.appspot.com/s/phishing.html"}
    }
  ]
}


Example if safe:

{}

if "matches" in result:
    print("⚠️ Dangerous website detected:", result["matches"])
else:
    print("✅ Safe website")


If "matches" exists in the result, the site is dangerous (phishing/malware).

Otherwise, the site is safe.

Prints the result in the terminal.

🔹 How It Works in Practice

Replace API_KEY with your actual Google API key.

Run the script in VS Code:

python app.py


If the site is phishing → prints:

⚠️ Dangerous website detected: [{'threatType': 'SOCIAL_ENGINEERING', ...}]


If safe → prints:

✅ Safe website


✅ So this code is a ready-to-use phishing/malware checker using Google’s database.




```
import requests
import json

API_KEY = "YOUR_GOOGLE_API_KEY"  # get from Google Cloud Console

url_to_check = "http://testsafebrowsing.appspot.com/s/phishing.html"

safe_browsing_url = f"https://safebrowsing.googleapis.com/v4/threatMatches:find?key={API_KEY}"

payload = {
    "client": {
        "clientId": "yourcompanyname",
        "clientVersion": "1.0"
    },
    "threatInfo": {
        "threatTypes": ["MALWARE", "SOCIAL_ENGINEERING", "POTENTIALLY_HARMFUL_APPLICATION", "THREAT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"],
        "platformTypes": ["ANY_PLATFORM"],
        "threatEntryTypes": ["URL"],
        "threatEntries": [
            {"url": url_to_check}
        ]
    }
}

response = requests.post(safe_browsing_url, json=payload)
result = response.json()

if "matches" in result:
    print("⚠️ Dangerous website detected:", result["matches"])
else:
    print("✅ Safe website")

```

